1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,514
Hi, I'm Max.

2
00:00:01,514 --> 00:00:08,962
Purser lets AI agents pay company bills, but only within limits the CFO signs with Face ID.

3
00:00:08,962 --> 00:00:12,905
A limit in a prompt is only a request.

4
00:00:12,905 --> 00:00:18,600
Here the agent proposes, the CFO signs, and the payment rails enforce it.

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:25,600
In the main run on 3 November, three Claude agents made 24 decisions.

6
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,400
Past a limit, an agent only proposes.

7
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,800
The CFO signs the exact terms.

8
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:35,600
Airwallex and Metal each hold the limit again, on their own side.

9
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:50,400
This is the hands-on demo: your own test company, gone after 24 hours, with test money on a simulated bank.

10
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,800
An invoice for 1,850 euros comes in.

11
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:59,200
The screen says who read it and what the checks found.

12
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:02,800
The CFO signs the exact terms with Face ID.

13
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:05,600
Change one cent, and it is refused.

14
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,800
On Metal, the agent's limit now lives in a passkey account.

15
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:43,200
The account checks the signatures itself, on chain: the CFO's passkey, on an iPhone with Face ID, and a second approver, here a labelled test passkey.

16
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:55,600
The agent paid 5 cents inside its mandate.

17
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:59,200
Then 6 cents, over the cap: refused on chain.

18
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:04,400
Both owners signed a higher cap, and the same 6 cents went through.

19
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:15,600
On Airwallex, each agent has its own card.

20
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:20,000
Airwallex itself declined a simulated 45 euro charge, over the limit.

21
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:28,800
Through Visa Intelligent Commerce and Airwallex's Airi, Claude chose the rail.

22
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:33,200
A 45 euro purchase above the limit waited for Face ID.

23
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:38,400
The signed terms' hash sits in Airi's mandate and in Airwallex's payment record.

24
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,400
Two locks on one payout.

25
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:48,400
Purser's, signed with a test passkey, and Airwallex's own approval.

26
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:52,800
The payout waited at Airwallex until the owner approved it there.

27
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:55,600
Then it was paid, with simulated settlement.

28
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:05,000
The books keep themselves.

29
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:14,200
In a month of a test company's 20 invoices, Claude read each one live and chose its account, VAT code and cost centre.

30
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:19,000
Code checked every choice before it was booked, and the books balance.

31
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:34,000
This is Purser Cloud's console for a test company: the overview, its agents, invoices and books, transactions and tokenisation.

32
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,200
It reads and manages, and it never pays.

33
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:41,200
Payments are approved on the CFO's phone with Face ID.

34
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:51,600
Every line of this film has its record.

35
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:56,800
The proof page lists what Purser guarantees, who enforces it, and the evidence.

36
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:13,600
What is not done: in the Visa sandbox, a credential reused on a bigger payment was not refused.

37
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:16,000
There, only Purser holds the limit.

38
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,200
Settlement is simulated.

39
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,058
Agents do the work.

40
00:04:22,058 --> 00:04:24,845
The CFO signs only the exceptions.

41
00:04:24,845 --> 00:04:31,348
Card limits, payouts and mandates: our code checks them, and the rail checks again.

42
00:04:31,348 --> 00:04:33,206
Purser, for Kit 11.

43
00:04:33,206 --> 00:04:34,600
Try it yourself.
